{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2189-06-01 23:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having severe abdominal pain since last night?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2189-06-01 23:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it's sharp and in my upper belly, left of center. It gets worse when I eat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2189-06-01 23:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you haven't passed gas or had a bowel movement since this morning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2189-06-01 23:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, nothing. That’s really unusual for me. I usually have many loose stools every day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2189-06-01 23:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history of sclerosing mesenteritis and multiple bowel obstructions, this could be another partial blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2189-06-01 23:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It feels just like my past obstructions. Is that what the X-ray showed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2189-06-01 23:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The abdominal X-ray shows multiple air-fluid levels, which suggests ileus or partial obstruction. But stool is still moving into your rectum, so it’s not a complete blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2189-06-01 23:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s the plan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2189-06-01 23:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you NPO—nothing by mouth—for now. We’ll insert a nasogastric tube to decompress your stomach and bowels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2189-06-01 23:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had that before. It’s uncomfortable, but I know it helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2189-06-01 23:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll also start IV fluids and give you pain and nausea meds. Your labs show low calcium and magnesium, so we’ll replace those."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2189-06-01 23:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I’m just glad it’s not worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2189-06-02 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your NG tube drained about 460 mL yesterday, and you had three bowel movements. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2189-06-02 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel a bit better. Is the blockage clearing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2189-06-02 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It looks like it. We’ll try clamping the NG tube today to see if you can tolerate it off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2189-06-02 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I start drinking water if it goes well?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2189-06-02 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start with a clear liquid diet if you don’t have nausea or pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2189-06-03 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news—you passed the clamp trial. We’re removing the NG tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2189-06-03 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s a relief. I hated that tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2189-06-03 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting you on clear liquids and will advance to full liquids, then soft foods."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2189-06-03 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my IV? It’s been hard to keep it in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2189-06-03 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve scheduled a PICC line placement today for better access, since you’ve had trouble in the past."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2189-06-03 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had those before. Is it done with ultrasound?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2189-06-03 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and fluoroscopy to guide it. It’ll go into your right arm and end in a large vein near your heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2189-06-04 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The PICC was placed successfully in your right axillary vein."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2189-06-04 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But my arm is burning—sharp pain from shoulder to hand. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2189-06-04 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We consulted neurology. They think it’s nerve irritation from the line placement, not damage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2189-06-04 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it go away? Shouldn’t they pull the line?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2189-06-04 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They don’t think removing it will help. It should improve with time. We’ll start a lidocaine patch and increase your gabapentin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2189-06-04 13:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust them. Just want the pain to ease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2189-06-04 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re also advancing you to a regular diet today. You’ve been stooling regularly, which is excellent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2189-06-04 13:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I ate toast and applesauce earlier—no nausea. That’s progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2189-06-04 13:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Definitely. Your labs are stable—hemoglobin is 9.0, and electrolytes are normal now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2189-06-04 13:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still low hemoglobin, but I’ve always been anemic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2189-06-04 13:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, chronic anemia from your bowel issues. We’re not concerned as long as it’s stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2189-06-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. Pain is controlled, you’re eating regular food, and your arm pain is improving with the lidocaine patch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2189-06-05 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been walking the halls too. Feeling stronger."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2189-06-05 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning if all stays on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2189-06-05 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What meds will I go home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2189-06-05 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue your usual meds. We’re increasing gabapentin to 1200 mg twice daily for your arm nerve pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2189-06-05 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the lidocaine patch?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2189-06-05 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, one patch daily on your right arm as needed. We’re also switching from pantoprazole to famotidine for stomach protection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2189-06-05 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that because of my liver history?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2189-06-05 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partly, and famotidine is safer long-term. You’ll keep taking rivaroxaban for your DVT history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2189-06-05 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know—no NSAIDs, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2189-06-05 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Stick to acetaminophen or your prescribed oxycodone for pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2189-06-06 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go home. Your bowel function has returned, and you’re stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2189-06-06 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m so glad. What should I watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2189-06-06 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call if you have increasing pain, vomiting, or can’t pass stool or gas. Also, monitor your arm for worsening pain or swelling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2189-06-06 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow up with my GI doctor?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2189-06-06 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, with Dr. ___ as planned. Take care, and we’re glad you’re feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2189-06-06 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I really appreciate everything."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2189-06-01 23:37:00",
    "admission_end": "2189-06-06 08:25:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a complex history including sclerosing mesenteritis, chronic small bowel obstructions, and line-associated DVTs presented with acute epigastric pain, nausea, and inability to pass stool or flatus, consistent with a partial bowel obstruction. Abdominal imaging showed air-fluid levels without a transition point, suggesting ileus. She was managed conservatively with NPO status, NG tube decompression, IV fluids, and electrolyte repletion. Her symptoms improved by hospital day 2 with return of bowel function, allowing NG tube removal and advancement to a regular diet. Due to difficult IV access, a PICC line was placed, which led to transient right arm neuropathic pain managed with a lidocaine patch and increased gabapentin. She remained stable, ambulatory, and pain-controlled, and was discharged home with follow-up plans. No signs of recurrent obstruction or complications were noted at discharge.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Anemia in other chronic diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Long term (current) use of antithrombotics/antiplatelets",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease with esophagitis",
      "Personal history of other venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Other disturbances of skin sensation",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Unspecified viral hepatitis C without hepatic coma",
      "Functional dyspepsia",
      "Nonrheumatic mitral (valve) prolapse",
      "Unspecified asthma, uncomplicated",
      "Tachycardia, unspecified",
      "Other specified disorders of bone density and structure, unspecified site",
      "Personal history of transient ischemic attack (TIA), and cerebral infarction without residual deficits",
      "Personal history of urinary (tract) infections",
      "Postprocedural hypothyroidism",
      "Other long term (current) drug therapy",
      "Migraine, unspecified, not intractable, without status migrainosus"
    ]
  }
}
